      "writtenOn": "2026-10-06T14:57:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Probably not blocking but this is what gemini was saying:\n\n`Pipeline Cache Miss Risk: At runtime, DrawPass still sets DepthStencilFlags::kDepth because fDepthStencilFlags uses step-\u003eusesDepth() (which is still true for all these steps). Therefore, at runtime, draws are recorded with depth attachments. Precompiling them without depth for non-depth render passes compiles pipelines that will never match runtime draws, leading to runtime compilation jank and cache misses.`",
      "revId": "e2c0bb6af95fdf80c99d27d8241862f7f7fb4b18",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
